numbers.sort(Integer::compareTo);
Descending:
numbers.sort(Collections.reverseOrder());
132. How do you remove duplicates from ArrayList?
Simple solution
List<String> list = new ArrayList<>();

list.add("Java");
list.add("Selenium");
list.add("Java");

List<String> unique =
        new ArrayList<>(new LinkedHashSet<>(list));

System.out.println(unique);

Output:

[Java, Selenium]
Why LinkedHashSet?

Because it:

removes duplicates
preserves insertion order
If order doesn't matter:
List<String> unique =
        new ArrayList<>(new HashSet<>(list));
133. How do you convert List to Set?
List<String> list =
        Arrays.asList("Java", "Selenium", "Java");

Set<String> set = new HashSet<>(list);

If you want to preserve insertion order:

Set<String> set = new LinkedHashSet<>(list);
134. How do you iterate Map?
Method 1 — entrySet() ⭐ Preferred
Map<Integer, String> map = new HashMap<>();

map.put(1, "Java");
map.put(2, "Selenium");

for (Map.Entry<Integer, String> entry : map.entrySet()) {

    System.out.println(
        entry.getKey() + " = " + entry.getValue()
    );
}
Method 2 — keySet()
for (Integer key : map.keySet()) {
    System.out.println(key + " = " + map.get(key));
}
Method 3 — forEach()
map.forEach((key, value) ->
    System.out.println(key + " = " + value)
);
Interview answer:

If I need both key and value, I prefer entrySet() because it directly gives me both.

135. How do you find duplicate values using HashMap? 🔴

Very common coding question.

Suppose:

String[] names = {
    "Java",
    "Selenium",
    "Java",
    "API",
    "Selenium"
};

We can maintain a frequency map.

Map<String, Integer> frequency = new HashMap<>();

for (String name : names) {

    frequency.put(
        name,
        frequency.getOrDefault(name, 0) + 1
    );
}

for (Map.Entry<String, Integer> entry : frequency.entrySet()) {

    if (entry.getValue() > 1) {
        System.out.println(entry.getKey());
    }
}

Output:

Java
Selenium
How it works

First occurrence:

Java → 1

Second occurrence:

Java → 2

Then:

if (value > 1)

means it is duplicated.

